# ==========================================================================
# PageFly Design — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. On Vercel, set these in
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# Nothing here has a working default in production: the two REQUIRED variables
# below fail loudly rather than falling back, because a fallback secret in a
# public repository is the same as no secret at all.
# ==========================================================================

# ---- REQUIRED -------------------------------------------------------------

# Signs the session cookies. Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Not required to get running. Without it:
#   - on serverless, the key is derived from the platform's project identifiers,
#     which every instance of the deployment shares, so sessions work
#   - elsewhere, a random key is generated and written next to the data store
#
# Set it anyway before this is public: a derived key can be recomputed by anyone
# with access to the Vercel project, and only a real secret survives moving hosts.
SESSION_SECRET=

# Postgres. Vercel Postgres, Neon and Supabase all work unchanged — it is the
# same protocol. Vercel's own integration sets POSTGRES_URL for you, which is
# also read.
DATABASE_URL=

# ---- OR: run without Postgres, on ONE server ------------------------------
# Set PFD_STORE=file to keep everything in a JSON file instead. Correct on a
# single-instance VPS with a persistent disk, and the fastest way to get running.
#
# NEVER set this on Vercel or behind more than one process: serverless instances
# neither share a disk nor keep one, so each would answer from its own copy and
# merchants would watch their library appear and disappear.
#
# PFD_STORE=file
# PFD_DB_FILE=/var/lib/pagefly-design/store.json

# ---- ALLOWLIST SHEET ------------------------------------------------------
# Pick ONE of the three. The sheet holds merchant email addresses, so option 2
# is the least private of them — see lib/sheet.ts.

# 1. Service account (recommended). Create one in Google Cloud, enable the
#    Sheets API, then share the sheet with the service account's email as
#    Viewer. Paste the whole JSON key on one line.
SHEET_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# 2. Any URL that returns CSV, including File > Share > Publish to web.
#    WARNING: publishing that sheet exposes every merchant email to anyone with
#    the link. Prefer option 1 or 3 for the real list.
ALLOWLIST_SHEET_CSV_URL=

# 3. Push model — n8n reads the sheet with your existing Google credential and
#    POSTs the rows to /api/admin/sync with this value in an x-sync-secret
#    header. No Google credentials on our side at all.
SYNC_SECRET=

# 4. Or none of the above: sign in to /design/admin → Users → "Paste the sheet
#    instead", and paste the rows straight out of Google Sheets. Nothing to
#    configure, and the sheet stays private.

# Which sheet and tab to read (only used by options 1 and 2).
ALLOWLIST_SHEET_ID=13gh6ymdVQLzeQARArytZWqWmNA6uAd4Si_kaum1fOcw
ALLOWLIST_SHEET_TAB=User Beta

# Page allowance for a store whose "Số page" cell is empty or unparseable.
DEFAULT_PAGE_LIMIT=30

# ---- REVIEWS --------------------------------------------------------------

# The n8n webhook that writes the star rating into the sheet. Reviews are saved
# to the database first and forwarded second, so leaving this unset loses
# nothing: rows stay with forwarded = false and can be replayed later.
REVIEW_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional. Sent as x-webhook-secret so the n8n workflow can reject anything
# that is not us.
REVIEW_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ---- ADMIN ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Defaults to admin / pf123456 — the pair specified for launch. Both are weak
# and shared; override them before anyone outside the team can reach
# /design/admin. Compared server-side only, so they never reach the browser.
ADMIN_USERNAME=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---- AI GENERATION --------------------------------------------------------
# Unset means page copy comes from the deterministic generator: no model, no
# tokens, no cost. That is a valid way to run — the app is complete without it.
#
# Set one of these and the model rewrites each page's copy for the merchant's
# actual store. Structure, layout and images stay deterministic either way.
AI_PROVIDER=anthropic
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# AI_PROVIDER=deepseek
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Override the model. Defaults: claude-haiku-4-5 / deepseek-v4-flash
# AI_MODEL=

# ---- free design ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# The design step reads the merchant's input and nothing else. Stage 1 is
# skipped whole: no pattern library, no per-trade block naming this store's
# hero, no ban list, no fixed order of roles, no pinned buy box or closing
# form, and no section count. The design model decides how many sections the
# page has, what each one is, what order they run in, and everything inside
# them, and hands that straight to the build model.
#
# What it still gets is what the page has to physically be: the elements
# PageFly can carry, the CSS the export can carry, and the shape of the answer.
# Those are not taste — a design using `position: absolute` is a mockup of a
# page the merchant will not get.
#
# NOT AN ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE. It is `FREE_DESIGN` in
# `lib/design/sectionSpec.ts`, a constant, and setting it here does nothing.
# Decided in the repository on purpose: the value is reviewed, it is in the
# history, and the running server cannot be doing something the source does not
# say. Turning it off is editing that line and shipping.
#
# COSTS, so they are not a surprise: one long call per PAGE rather than one
# short call for the whole deck; the training sections stop being looked up,
# because there is no pattern id to look them up by; and three of the audit's
# checks go quiet for the same reason.

# ---- struct-v2: the deck plan --------------------------------------------
#
# One call that designs the whole deck — how many sections each page has, which
# ones, in what order, which band is the signature, which invert, how much room
# each gets, which may carry a photograph, what moves, and what goes inside
# each band. Off unless this is exactly "true"; unset, a build runs as it
# always has.
# USE_DECK_PLAN=true
#
# WHO DESIGNS IS NO LONGER SET HERE. `DESIGN_PROVIDER` and `DESIGN_MODEL` are
# constants in `lib/ai/provider.ts`, and setting them here does nothing.
#
# They used to be read from the environment, and the deployment never set them.
# A role that names no provider of its own inherits the default one entirely, so
# the design stages resolved to DeepSeek while every measurement of them was
# taken on a laptop that did set them. Nobody could see it until /api/health
# started reporting `designProvider` and `designModel`.
#
#   DESIGN_API_KEY=          # still an env var, and optional: a different key at
#                            # the same vendor is how an expensive model stays
#                            # legible on a bill. Falls back to ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
#
# Without a key of either name, `providerName("design")` is "none" and the design
# stage says so rather than quietly running on something cheaper.
# DESIGN_API_KEY=
